Station T-32, located in survey area T, consists of a six-layer sequence. The resistivity profile begins at 184.7 $\Omega\cdot$m, increases to a peak of 735.3 $\Omega\cdot$m in layer 2, and then steadily decreases through layer 3 (503.9 $\Omega\cdot$m) and layer 4 (56.6 $\Omega\cdot$m). Layer 5 reaches a minimum of 43.3 $\Omega\cdot$m before layer 6 rises sharply to 520.0 $\Omega\cdot$m.

According to the curve-type notation rules, this sequence generates a KQQH curve. Please note that the existing file classification of "A-type" is inaccurate and does not align with the interpreted resistivity values provided in the model.

